            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>How long is the train from Portland to Boston?</h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes ~2h45 - 3h30, depending on service and stops.</p>

            <h3>What is the fastest train from Portland to Boston?</h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Downeaster, which completes the journey in approximately 2 hours and 45 minutes with direct service.</p>

            <h3>How much does a train ticket from Portland to Boston cost?</h3>

            <p>Early Booking: $30-$45</p>

            <p>Standard Fare: $45-$65</p>

            <p>Last-Minute / Flexible: $65-$80+</p>

            <h3>Are there direct trains from Portland to Boston?</h3>
            <p>Yes, all Amtrak Downeaster trains run direct, so there is no need for transfers.</p>

            <h3>What amenities are available onboard?</h3>
            <p> Trains offer comfortable seating, Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets, a cafe car, and luggage storage.</p>

            <h3>Is train travel faster than driving?</h3>
            <p> Driving may take ~2h30 - 3h15 depending on traffic, while the train provides a predictable, stress-free, and scenic journey.</p>

            <h3>Can you travel from Portland to Boston in one day?</h3>
            <p> Yes, the route is suitable for same-day trips, but early departures are recommended to maximize time in Boston.</p>

            <h3>Which station in Portland do trains depart from?</h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from the Portland Transportation Center in downtown Portland. Some airport connections from Portland International Jetport (PWM) exist but require extra planning.</p>

            <h3>Which station do trains arrive at in Boston?</h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at Boston North Station, conveniently located in the city center and accessible by public transport.</p>

            <h3>Is Business Class worth it?</h3>
            <p> Yes, Business Class provides extra legroom, a quieter environment, and priority boarding-ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the ~2h45 - 3h30 journey. </p>




